      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture. I'll improve the test by:\n1. Removing the large block of unused imports\n2. Removing unused constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `TEST`)\n3. Replacing the magic literal `2008` with `YEAR_LEAP.getValue()` to connect it to the declared constantThe improved test compiled successfully. The changes made were: removed ~45 unused imports, dropped three unused constants (`YEAR_STANDARD`, `STANDARD_YEAR_LENGTH`, `TEST`), replaced the magic literal `2008` with `YEAR_LEAP.getValue()` to tie the test date to the named constant, and added a one-line comment explaining the intent of `test_now_clock_leapYear`."
